# The first machine the campaign asks anybody to own, and deliberately not a
# very good one.
#
# Iron Valley wants ore powder, which is two crushings and a milling, and the
# only interesting decision in the whole line is the drive train. A crusher
# will not take a drive turning at speed 6 and a mill will not take one turning
# slower than 4, so no single motor can serve both -- each crusher gets a motor
# through a gearbox, and the mill gets one straight.
#
# And there the design stops being adequate. A mill wants 80 rotary and a motor
# makes 54, so the mill runs at about two thirds and everything upstream backs
# up behind it. That is on purpose: this is the machine a player is handed, and
# the second motor it obviously wants is the first thing anybody will do to it.
#
#   drive train        180 MW off the grid, for 67 powder a second
#   the mill           54 rotary of the 80 it asked for
#   the obvious fix    another motor, a shaft, and a look at the gearboxes

machine "Powder Line"
brief crush

inlet     I1  at 0,0    draws ore

crusher   C1  at 3,0
crusher   C2  at 7,0
mill      MI1 at 11,0
outlet    O1  at 15,0

gearbox   GB1 at 3,4    ratio 4
motor     MO1 at 3,7
mains     M1  at 3,10

gearbox   GB2 at 7,4    ratio 4
motor     MO2 at 7,7
mains     M2  at 7,10

motor     MO3 at 11,4
mains     M3  at 11,7

wire M1.power -> MO1.power
wire MO1.rotary -> GB1.in
wire GB1.out -> C1.drive

wire M2.power -> MO2.power
wire MO2.rotary -> GB2.in
wire GB2.out -> C2.drive

wire M3.power -> MO3.power
wire MO3.rotary -> MI1.drive

wire I1.out -> C1.in
wire C1.out -> C2.in
wire C2.out -> MI1.in
wire MI1.out -> O1.solid
